CORE
definition.c caller.c
--replace-call-with-contract f
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition\.1\] line 6 Check requires clause of f in main: SUCCESS$
^\[f\.precondition\.2\] line 6 Check requires clause of f in main: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The caller's translation unit declares a larger constant [static N] minimum
than the contract's translation unit. Linking keeps the larger minimum on the
function and refreshes the generated requires clause of the contract, so
legacy contract replacement checks eight elements rather than four.
